  "note": "Triennial election of Londonderry Corporation (all twenty members: five aldermen and fifteen councillors), due Wednesday 20 May 1964: no poll. Two Independents nominated for the North Ward, Raymond Wolseley and Mrs Winifred Haslett, withdrew their nominations, leaving the official Unionist and Nationalist nominees unopposed (Derry Journal, 8 May 1964, p. 15). The Returning Officer's notice of result lists the five aldermen and fifteen councillors as duly elected with no votes recorded (Derry Journal, 26 May 1964, p. 7). O'Hare (Eugene O'Hare) was the new Nationalist councillor (Derry Journal, 8 May 1964, p. 15). Returned unopposed."
